cartridge "CHENILLE/J-F SEHAN + C KOSNIOWSKI/1984"

' CHENILLE - one ColecoVision game made from two Oric games:
'   "Chenille" by Jean-Francois Sehan ("L'Oric a l'affiche", Editions du
'   P.S.I., 1984) and "Snake" by Czes Kosniowski ("Games to Play on Your
'   Oric-1", Shiva, 1983, game 20).
' Adapted by Amy & Claude, Amy Studio 2026. Built by build.py from this
' file, ../_common/amy/core.alexis, pages.txt, art.py and music/*.txt.
'
' THE GAME: a caterpillar crawls without stopping; the joystick turns it.
' It grows by one ring with every critter it swallows (both books). The
' critters are Sehan's two sorts: the white ones with big ears give a bonus,
' the pink ones with raised arms take one away - and eating one with no
' bonus left loses the caterpillar (Sehan's twist). Eat every critter to
' clear the leaf; the next leaf has more of them (Sehan: E = E + 10).
' Kosniowski's obstructions are the rocks: some lie on the leaf from level
' 2, and from level 3 every pink critter eaten makes one more rock fall from
' the sky (his FOOD routine added three rocks per meal). The fence, a rock
' or the caterpillar's own body is the end of it (both books).
'
' CONTROLS: joystick only. Title: up/down choose, left/right change the
' starting level, a button confirms.
'
' LIBERTIES (listed for Amy):
' - Joystick in four absolute directions (Kosniowski's cursor keys) rather
'   than Sehan's left/right turns; going straight back is ignored (both
'   books made it impossible or fatal).
' - Three caterpillars (lives); a death restarts the same leaf, new layout.
'   Sehan's game ended at the first mistake, Kosniowski's at "WELL DONE".
' - Level 1 = Sehan's first leaf (10 critters, half of each), no rocks, a
'   calm crawl (12 frames a cell). Tables for levels 1-16: +2 critters a
'   level (Sehan: +10, too steep with a growing body), 3 to 24 rocks at the
'   start, a crawl of 12 down to 4 frames a cell; falling rocks: one per
'   anti-bonus from level 3, two from level 8; one per bonus too from
'   level 5, two from level 11 (Kosniowski: three per meal).
' - A falling rock is seen falling (4 pixels a frame, up to 3/4 s), never
'   lands within 8 cells of the head (as chosen), never next to another
'   rock, a critter or the fence (no pockets), and crumbles if the
'   caterpillar is on its cell when it lands.
' - The bonus count is shown as icons (9 at most; more are kept, so a leaf
'   can always be finished: there are as many bonuses as anti-bonuses).
' - Colour, animation, music and sound effects are new; the Oric's PING,
'   ZAP, SHOOT and EXPLODE and Kosniowski's red PAPER flash are the cues.

